WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.137
The smallest nonzero rank is one.

2
00:00:06.137 --> 00:00:08.884
Multiply a column by a row

3
00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:13.103
the drone's first button u, one, two, one

4
00:00:13.103 --> 00:00:16.340
times r one, the first row of R.

5
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.688
Each row of the product is an

6
00:00:19.791 --> 00:00:23.927
entry of u times r one: one times r one

7
00:00:23.927 --> 00:00:28.579
two times r one, two, zero, four, minus two

8
00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:31.370
and one times r one again.

9
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.765
Every row is a multiple of r one and

10
00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.303
every column a multiple of u

11
00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:39.757
the row space and the column

12
00:00:39.841 --> 00:00:41.195
space are lines.

13
00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:42.041
Rank one.

14
00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:45.678
In the plane you can see it: P three, two

15
00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.032
four, one, two.

16
00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:50.162
Its columns, two, one and four, two

17
00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:51.600
lie on one line.

18
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.935
Every rank r matrix is a sum

19
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.100
of r rank one pieces.

20
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.575
For the drone

21
00:00:58.575 --> 00:01:02.609
the second piece is the second button v

22
00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:06.348
one, three, two, times the row r two

23
00:01:06.348 --> 00:01:09.300
which is zero, one, one, one.

24
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.930
Add the two pieces row by row.

25
00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.663
Row one: one, zero, two

26
00:01:15.663 --> 00:01:19.598
minus one plus zero, one, one, one.

27
00:01:19.598 --> 00:01:22.441
Row two: two, zero, four

28
00:01:22.441 --> 00:01:27.032
minus two plus zero, three, three, three.

29
00:01:27.032 --> 00:01:29.984
Row three: one, zero, two

30
00:01:29.984 --> 00:01:33.919
minus one plus zero, two, two, two.

31
00:01:33.919 --> 00:01:35.450
The sum is A.

32
00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.046
This is A equals C times R zero

33
00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:41.987
the pivot columns of A times

34
00:01:42.089 --> 00:01:44.320
the nonzero rows of R

35
00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:46.957
one piece for each pivot.

36
00:01:46.957 --> 00:01:51.319
Now a question: is the sum of two rank one

37
00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.956
matrices always rank two?

38
00:01:53.956 --> 00:01:55.680
Pause and think.

39
00:01:59.260 --> 00:01:59.529
No.

40
00:01:59.529 --> 00:02:03.387
Take P one: its first column is one, zero

41
00:02:03.387 --> 00:02:06.168
and its second column is zero.

42
00:02:06.168 --> 00:02:09.577
Take P two: its first column is zero

43
00:02:09.577 --> 00:02:12.807
and its second column is zero, one.

44
00:02:12.807 --> 00:02:14.512
Each has rank one

45
00:02:14.512 --> 00:02:17.293
but their sum is the identity

46
00:02:17.293 --> 00:02:20.523
whose columns span the whole plane

47
00:02:20.523 --> 00:02:21.420
rank two.

48
00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.537
The sum can also stay rank one.

49
00:02:24.537 --> 00:02:28.464
P three has columns two, one and four, two.

50
00:02:28.464 --> 00:02:32.391
P four has columns one, zero and two, zero.

51
00:02:32.391 --> 00:02:36.140
Their sum has columns three, one and six

52
00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.282
two: again on one line.

53
00:02:38.372 --> 00:02:40.603
And P three minus P three

54
00:02:40.692 --> 00:02:43.370
is the zero matrix, rank zero.

55
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.676
So adding rank one matrices

56
00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:47.053
can leave the set

57
00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:49.517
and the zero matrix is not in it

58
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:52.560
the rank one matrices are not a subspace.

59
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.459
Matrices can be added and

60
00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:57.407
scaled like vectors

61
00:02:57.499 --> 00:02:59.726
so a set of matrices can

62
00:02:59.818 --> 00:03:01.859
be a vector space too.

63
00:03:01.952 --> 00:03:04.178
Read a two by two matrix

64
00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:07.146
as its four entries a, b, c, d

65
00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:09.836
all two by two matrices form

66
00:03:09.928 --> 00:03:12.340
a space of dimension four.

67
00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.474
Inside it, the symmetric matrices

68
00:03:15.474 --> 00:03:18.257
with b equal to c: one condition

69
00:03:18.257 --> 00:03:21.778
so three free numbers and dimension three.

70
00:03:21.778 --> 00:03:24.316
The upper triangular matrices

71
00:03:24.316 --> 00:03:27.100
with c equal to zero: also three.

72
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.702
And the diagonal matrices, both conditions

73
00:03:30.702 --> 00:03:31.930
dimension two.

74
00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:34.210
Back to the café.

75
00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:37.410
Four regulars rate five drinks

76
00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:40.110
and each rating comes from

77
00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:42.010
two hidden tastes

78
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:45.610
how much a customer likes sweet, p

79
00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:49.710
and likes bitter, q, times how sweet, g

80
00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.110
and how bitter, h, each drink is.

81
00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.584
So the table is p times g transpose

82
00:03:56.674 --> 00:03:58.905
plus q times h transpose

83
00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.780
two rank one pieces.

84
00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.833
Ana likes sweet twice

85
00:04:02.833 --> 00:04:06.403
so her row of the first piece is two g.

86
00:04:06.403 --> 00:04:09.171
Ben likes bitter twice: two h.

87
00:04:09.171 --> 00:04:10.599
Add the pieces

88
00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:13.991
and the four by five table X appears.

89
00:04:13.991 --> 00:04:17.740
Twenty numbers, but eighteen describe it.

90
00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.099
All four subspaces mean something.

91
00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:25.082
Ana plus Ben minus two Caro is the zero row

92
00:04:25.082 --> 00:04:27.294
two plus two minus four

93
00:04:27.294 --> 00:04:30.657
zero plus four minus four, and so on

94
00:04:30.657 --> 00:04:31.542
all zero.

95
00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:35.436
And cocoa's column is twice tea's, so zero

96
00:04:35.436 --> 00:04:36.941
zero, zero, two

97
00:04:36.941 --> 00:04:39.684
minus one is in the nullspace.

98
00:04:39.684 --> 00:04:42.959
At scale, take a thousand customers

99
00:04:42.959 --> 00:04:46.145
five hundred drinks and ten tastes.

100
00:04:46.145 --> 00:04:49.862
The pieces need fifteen thousand numbers

101
00:04:49.862 --> 00:04:53.490
and the full table needs half a million.

102
00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:54.337
So

103
00:04:54.337 --> 00:04:58.166
a rank one matrix is a column times a row

104
00:04:58.166 --> 00:05:01.105
and its columns lie on one line.

105
00:05:01.105 --> 00:05:04.934
A rank r matrix is a sum of r such pieces

106
00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:07.160
A equals C times R zero

107
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.030
one piece per pivot.

108
00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.604
Rank one matrices are not a subspace

109
00:05:12.604 --> 00:05:14.956
one plus one can make two.

110
00:05:14.956 --> 00:05:18.790
Your turn: write the matrix T from exercise

111
00:05:18.877 --> 00:05:21.491
three as a column times a row.

112
00:05:21.491 --> 00:05:24.540
Next lecture: graphs and networks.
